// A chained function's fingerprints: one per segment, not one per function.
//
// Each chain block, and the initial function, is its own unit for duplicate
// checking, so a chain that happens to match a function elsewhere is reported
// -- which is the point, since it means the chain was not really a
// continuation of anything.
//
// The split is made on the body's NODE LIST, at the `chain` marker that
// front/parse/decl/func/sig/chain/tail.id pushes, and deliberately not by
// splitting the finished canonical string on the seam `cst4` emits. A string
// literal canonicalises as its text verbatim (`"S" + s1_of(id)`,
// ../../../expr/expr.id), so a program with a `|` inside a string could forge
// a segment boundary -- and `|` is the field separator in the compiler's own
// --calls format strings, so that is not a hypothetical program. A forged seam
// would make two unlike segments compare equal and report a duplicate against
// a legal program, the costliest mistake this checker can make.
//
// Every segment carries the function's signature, so two segments collide only
// when they agree on the signature as well as on the logic. A `native` has no
// body to segment and is fingerprinted by name instead: ./kind/native.id.
//
// The names here are deliberately unshared: `out`, `seg`, `sig` and `ps`
// already mean other things elsewhere in the tree, and a name keeps one type
// across the whole program (docs/PROJECT.md, checklist 6).

canon_segs(int id) {
  string[] segs_out = [];
  segs_kind(id, segs_out);
} return string[] segs_out;
given lz_o (22):(["()->int=>v0{d:int 0=I5}"])
given lz_o (23):(["()->int=>v0{d:int 0=I9}"])

// A function with a real body: its signature, then its segments.
segs_plain(int id, string[] segs_out) {
  string sigtext = segs_sig(id);
  segs_walk(id, sigtext, segs_out);
} return void;
given lz_o (22, []):() then calls segs_walk:[1]
given lz_o (23, []):() then calls segs_sig:[1]

// The accumulator starts empty and is flushed at every seam; the trailing
// flush is what emits the last segment, which no marker follows.
segs_walk(int id, string sigtext, string[] segs_out) {
  int[] cur = [];
  segs_loop(id, sigtext, cur, segs_out);
  segs_flush(sigtext, cur, segs_out);
} return void;
given lz_o (22, "S", []):() then calls segs_flush:[1]
given lz_o (23, "S", []):() then calls segs_loop:[1]
